From: ares-7.3.3-port <no-reply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: mediatek,mtk-xhci: add mediatek,mt6893-xhci

MT6893's USB3 DRD controller exposes its xHCI host as a child node.
The ares board devicetree describes it with the two-string pair

    compatible = "mediatek,mt6893-xhci", "mediatek,mtk-xhci";

so that the mainline xhci-mtk driver (whose of_match contains the
generic "mediatek,mtk-xhci" fallback) can bind without any driver-side
change. The schema's SoC-specific enum so far lists other MediaTek
SoCs only, so dtbs_check rejects the first string. Add it.

The child node is converted to mainline form: clocks/clock-names use a
single clk26m fixed-clock with "sys_ck", and vbus-supply /
vusb33-supply point at the board's fixed regulators. No other schema
change is needed.

Signed-off-by: ares-7.3.3-port <no-reply@localhost>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtk-xhci.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtk-xhci.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtk-xhci.yaml
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
       - enum:
           - mediatek,mt2701-xhci
           - mediatek,mt2712-xhci
+          - mediatek,mt6893-xhci
           - mediatek,mt7622-xhci
           - mediatek,mt7623-xhci
           - mediatek,mt7629-xhci
